import Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Ring.Lemmas
import H0mework.Physics.RLCResponse.Run

/-!
# Positive-resistance attraction of the dimensioned series-RLC transient

The free solution already generated by the dimensioned RLC compiler is the
homogeneous residual of a driven run.  This file proves that every such
residual tends to zero in physical time.  The proof uses the actual positive
compiled damping and arbitrary initial coordinates; it does not assume a
prefilled steady state or a bounded-time cutoff.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace SaturationMonoid
namespace NoIslandNoMagic
namespace Consciousness
namespace Immortality
